       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. At 1700 mg three times daily, the total is 5,100 mg/day, which is about double the maximum labeled dose of metformin immediate-release (2,550 mg/day). Metformin-associated lactic acidosis risk rises with excess dosing, so I want you to confirm the dose before it goes in.\n\nSome possibilities:\n- **850 mg TID** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum for IR). This is the most common intended dose for this regimen.\n- **500 mg TID** or another lower dose, if you're titrating.\n- **1700 mg TID** as written, if you intend this. It would be unusual for a 70 kg patient with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPlease tell me which dose you want, or confirm 1700 mg TID explicitly. I'll then enter it with route PO, three times daily with meals."
      }
